.TH SKELETON 1 "October 2026" "skeleton 26.10.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skeleton \- first-hour autopsy for ssh artifacts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skeleton
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skeleton
reads ssh artifacts from disk \(em keys, authorized_keys files, daemon and
client configs, known_hosts \- and scores what it finds. read-only, offline,
single static binary. built for the first hour of incident response on a
developer machine, when the question is which keys can open the host and
which of them look planted.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B keys
.I PATH...
inventory keys: algorithm, bits, sha256 fingerprint, passphrase state,
permissions. flags dsa, rsa below 2048 bits, unencrypted identities,
world-readable private keys.
.TP
.B authorized
.I FILE...
audit authorized_keys lines: caged vs uncaged keys, forced-command analysis
(network pullers, interpreter one-liners, proper SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND jails),
from= breadth, option tampering, duplicate keys across files.
.TP
.B config
.I FILE...
audit sshd_config or ssh_config (auto-detected): relocated
AuthorizedKeysFile, AuthorizedKeysCommand, PermitEmptyPasswords, weak
ciphers/kex/macs, StrictHostKeyChecking no, UserKnownHostsFile /dev/null,
odd Include paths, unknown keywords.
.TP
.B known
.I FILE...
.RB [ \-\-check
.IR HOST[,HOST] ]
audit known_hosts: verify |1| hashed entries by hmac-sha1, list
cert-authority and @revoked records, catch conflicting keys for the same
host pattern (torn tofu reset), duplicates, plaintext hostname sprawl.
.TP
.B sweep
.I ROOT...
.RB [ \-\-fresh
.IR N ]
hunt artifacts where they do not belong: authorized_keys outside a .ssh
directory or /etc/ssh, identities in scratch space (/tmp, /var/tmp,
/dev/shm, /run), .ssh/rc login hooks, legacy authorized_keys2,
world-writable .ssh directories, identical authorized_keys planted twice,
files touched within N days.
.TP
.B fp
.I PATH...
one fingerprint line per key, for timelines and tickets.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-json
single-line machine report: tool, version, command, score, band, forced
flag, findings with id, severity, weight, where, note.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
plain output even on a tty.
.TP
.B \-\-check
.B known
only: verify candidate hostnames against hashed entries.
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
.B sweep
only: note artifacts modified within the last N days.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
clean (score 0\-9)
.TP
.B 1
watch (10\-29)
.TP
.B 2
suspicious (30\-59)
.TP
.B 3
hostile (60+, or any forced-hostile finding)
.TP
.B 64
usage error
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
disable ansi output.
.TP
.B SKELETON_FORCE_COLOR
force ansi output even when redirected.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.ssh/authorized_keys, ~/.ssh/authorized_keys2, ~/.ssh/rc,
/etc/ssh/sshrc, /etc/ssh/sshd_config, ~/.ssh/known_hosts, /etc/ssh/ssh_known_hosts
.SH SEE ALSO
ssh(1), sshd(8), ssh-keygen(1)
.SH LICENSE
isc
